  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An ideal gas is held in a cylinder by a piston. The piston compresses the gas rapidly.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The average speed of the gas molecules increases because the gas molecules...<br/><br/></p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">have a smaller volume available in which they can move.</li><li data-label=\"B\">receive thermal energy transferred from outside the cylinder.</li><li data-label=\"C\">receive energy from the piston as they collide with it.</li><li data-label=\"D\">make more collisions every second with each other.</li></ol>"
  },
